{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"957d01f92e94978f","name":"card_unit_caproni_ca_133","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/units/card_unit_caproni_ca_133","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CAPRONI CA.133","text":"Your HQ gets +2 defense when you deploy or add a unit.","flavorText":"The Caproni Ca.133 was a rugged, three-engine transport aircraft and light bomber which served as the backbone of the Italian Regia Aeronautica from the mid-1930s through the early years of WWII. First flown in 1934 and introduced a year later, it was originally designed as a civilian airliner before being adapted for military service, a transition where its simplicity and reliability proved invaluable. Constructed with a mix of wood, steel tubing, and fabric, the Ca.133 was built to endure harsh, remote environments. This durability made it ideal for colonial warfare. It saw extensive action in Italian East Africa during the Second Italo-Abyssinian War, performing bombing, strafing, reconnaissance, and transport missions, often in the absence of significant air opposition. While armed with defensive machine guns and a respectable bomb load, the Ca.133 was equally vital as a utility aircraft, with variants configured for troop transport or as air ambulances. Although slow and vulnerable to modern fighters, its versatility ensured a long career, with over 500 units built and active service continuing throughout Africa and the Mediterranean during WWII.","faction":"Italy","type":"bomber","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_caproni_ca_133","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_caproni_ca_133_title","SourceString":"CAPRONI CA.133","LocalizedString":"CAPRONI CA.133"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_caproni_ca_133_text","SourceString":"Your HQ g